<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Şebinkarahisar</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Koloneia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Şebinkarahisar is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giresun">Giresun</a> province, north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, below a fortress on a high rock. Known in Byzantine times as Koloneia, it was taken by the Mengujekids after 1071 and later passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>. It was long known for its alum mines, and in 1915 its Armenian inhabitants resisted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deportation">deportation</a> in a siege.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sebinkarahisar.jpg" alt="Şebinkarahisar" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Esginmurat · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2020_Y%C4%B1l%C4%B1nda_%C3%A7ekilmi%C5%9F,_k%C4%B1%C5%9F%C4%B1n_%C5%9Eebinkarahisar%27dan_bir_g%C3%B6r%C3%BCn%C3%BCm.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
